## Getting started

    make run

The application will start on port {{.Port}}.{{if eq .AppType "web"}} Visit
http://localhost:{{.Port}} in your browser.{{else}} Send requests to
http://localhost:{{.Port}}.{{end}}
{{- if eq .ConfigSource "flags"}}

Configuration settings are read from command-line flags. Run the application
with --help to see every setting and its default value:

    go run ./cmd/{{.CmdDir}} --help
{{- else}}

Configuration settings are read from environment variables. The available
variables and their defaults are listed in the `run()` function in
`cmd/{{.CmdDir}}/main.go`.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Migrations}}

## Database migrations

SQL migrations live in `assets/migrations`. To apply them:

    make migrations/up

Other migration commands: `make migrations/down`, `make migrations/goto
version=N`, `make migrations/force version=N`, `make migrations/version`, and
`make migrations/new name=add_example_table` to create a new migration pair.

The database DSN defaults to `{{.Driver.ExampleDSN}}`; override it with the
`DB_DSN` make variable or the `--db-dsn` flag.
{{- end}}

## Admin commands

Run `make help` to list the admin commands, including `make audit` (tests,
vet, staticcheck, govulncheck), `make test/cover` (coverage report),
`make run/live` (live reloading) and `make tidy`.

## Structure

    assets/       Non-code assets{{if eq .AppType "web"}} (static files, HTML templates){{end}}{{if .Migrations}}, SQL migrations{{end}}
    cmd/{{.CmdDir}}/      Application-specific code: startup, routes, handlers, helpers
    internal/     Ancillary packages used by the application

The `application` struct in `cmd/{{.CmdDir}}/main.go` holds the application's
dependencies; handlers, helpers and middleware are methods on it. Everything
is designed to be edited — this is your code.
